WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.960
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.840
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.390
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.690
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:18.810
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.360
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:38.970
dokoka tooku de mimi wo sumashiteru hito ga iru
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:46.940
arayuru basho de sora wo miageteru hito ga iru
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:54.820
yozora no shita de kuchibue fuiteru bokutachi wa
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:02.530
kotoba mo nai mama yubi de tada seiza wo nazotteru
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:10.000
samugariya no yume tsumetai kimi no te
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:19.380
atatameru mahou wa hitotsu no michi wo shinjiru koto
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:28.140
houkigumo no mukou ni mitsuketa hitotsubu no hoshi wa
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:32.400
kagayaku hoshi demo kasukana hoshi demo
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.400
kimi dake no hikari
is the light of only you.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.140
mune no kumo no mukou ni mienai mama no michishirube
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.000
is a sign post that remains unseen.
mune no kumo no mukou ni mienai mama no michishirube

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:51.670
saa kono te wo hiraite ima nani wo shinjimasuka?
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.650
Pantasia’s main store’s new employee examination.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.840
After experiencing a lot of drama, Azuma
Kazuma and Kawachi Kyousuke

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.680
pulled out of the new employee examination
for their own reasons.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.530
It may be over for me,

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.590
but at the very least
I’ll complete this creation!

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.480
What?!

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:14.840
No way.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.960
I-It really...

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.460
It really came out!

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.160
The moon came out!

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.810
But Azusagawa Tsukino, who had discovered
Kazuma’s and Kawachi’s talent early on,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.950
decided to welcome the two of them to Pantasia’s southern Tokyo store,

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.210
which she manages herself.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.220
And now, it’s the first day of work today for
the two who have accepted her request.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.490
But the boy who possesses Solar Hands, Azuma Kazuma...

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.160
on the early morning of his
first day at work...

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.880
was frozen solid.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.560
Hihiin!!

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.480
Make a Delicious Bread!

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.520
I’m alive again!

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.250
I was about to freeze to death on my first day!

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.530
I owe you my life!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.110
Thank you!

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:13.450
Thank you!
I-I was just... going to take out the Danish
dough that we left in the fridge...

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.700
I-I was just... going to take out the Danish
dough that we left in the fridge...

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.950
B-By the way, who are you...?

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.700
Oh, I’m Azuma Kazuma.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.220
I’ll be counting on you from today. Nice to meet you!

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.500
A new employee, from today onwards...

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.210
I’m called Kinoshita Kageto.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.090
Right, nice to meet you!

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.600
S-So...

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:40.140
the guy in that gap over there, who’s already
reciting some kind of incantation,

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.810
is also new...?

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.640
Yeah, that’s Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.150
He’s a cheerful guy...

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.120
How is that?

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.360
This can’t be true.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.940
Why am I in a small-scale branch that only
seems to employ insignificant people?

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.150
My ambition...

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.110
was supposed to be kicking off my career

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.390
at Pantasia’s main store,
with over 200 employees,

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:02.050
and long lines of customers every day...

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.540
But instead... ah, but instead...

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:05.510
Well, that aside, why were you frozen?
But instead... ah, but instead...

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.070
Well, that aside, why were you frozen?

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.560
Oh, well, Tsukino...

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.380
T-This guy... addresses Tsukino-san
without an honorific title?!

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.060
What’s this about me?

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.780
Good morning.
You’re all here early.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.260
G-Good morning!

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.000
She gave me a task to make French
bread on my first day...

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:24.530
What?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.440
H-He used “koitsu” to address her?!

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.100
Yes.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:27.660
What?!

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.940
It’s our shop’s specialty product,
after all...

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:32.230
French bread.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.170
So, in order to make preparations,

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.420
I entered the refrigerator...

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.160
and the door shut behind me.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.420
I couldn’t open it from the inside.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.500
Well, you should be careful, too.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.010
Y-Yeah...

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.560
I shouldn’t have opened it.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.560
Well, it seems that the introductions have
been made already , so let’s start working.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.640
Today, I’ll have you make French bread.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.280
Okay!

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.270
There are over 10 main types
of French bread.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.280
I’d like you to make Parisian, which has a typical shape.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.940
Parisian?

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.190
It’s the name of a type of French bread.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.480
It can also be referred to as parikko.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.290
I see...
Note: “Parikko” literally means “child of Paris”,
used in reference to people from Paris.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.570
Length is 50 to 70cm.

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.490
Weight is about 500g,

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.300
and the coupe, or slits, are always in five cuts.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.210
French bread seems to be
a rival for <i>Japan</i>.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.790
I won’t lose!

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.300
<i>Japan</i>? What on earth is <i>Japan</i>?

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.750
I’d like to know, too.

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.560
Okay, <i>Japan</i> is...

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.420
to sum it up...

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.430
It’s bread that tastes better than rice.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.520
Better than rice?

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:43.180
For instance...

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.480
Our current task, French bread,
includes the country in its name.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.810
In other words, to the French, it’s the same as our rice.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.030
Well, I guess so...

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:57.070
But in Japan, there’s no bread worthy of our name.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.530
To tell the truth...

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:02.050
It’s proof that bread is losing to rice in Japan.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.790
That’s why it’s my dream
to create <i>Japan</i>,

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:11.050
a bread that would be loved by the Japanese as much as rice.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.670
T-That’s <i>Japan</i>...?

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:14.800
Wow...

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.760
That’s a dream on a grand scale.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:18.810
It’s wonderful.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.810
What, really?!

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:24.780
That’s right, this store isn’t as significant
in comparison to that place,

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.320
but outstanding people are gathered at the main store.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.180
If you have the manager’s recommendation,

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.870
there’s a chance you will be called
on to work at the main store.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:34.440
Please do your best.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.870
What did you say?!

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.160
Why didn’t you tell me that earlier?!

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.240
It’s troublesome if you don’t mention these
things in the beginning, dumbass.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.670
The one who said that was Tsukino-san...

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:52.580
In short, we need to make a bread
that impresses you, right?

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:53.720
Well, that’s...

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.340
This is my chance.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.480
A chance has returned to me.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:02.630
I’ll make a Parisian that astounds her,
and become invited to the main store.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.140
I’m going to become big!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:07.150
Yeah!

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.650
Big!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.150
<i>Japan</i>!

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:15.650
It’s really great to have a dream or goal.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.320
E-Even I...

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:21.670
have a dream... or two!

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:28.670
That’s it. Like making circles,
from the center outwards.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:32.180
You gradually mix the water and flour together.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.460
It seems kind of heavy.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.500
Huh?

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:38.180
The water does seem to be disappearing rapidly...

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.010
Perhaps I’ll add some more.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:41.810
Wow!

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.650
What water-absorbing power!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.400
T-This is...

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:53.860
This is like sprinkling water on a sunbaked desert.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.540
It’s because the gluten fibers inside the dough
are catching and absorbing the moisture.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:04.870
It’s impossible to create such high-quality
dough with normal fermentation.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.330
Those extraordinarily warm hands, called Solar Hands,

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.720
provide the ultimate environment
for the dough to ferment.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:20.350
Whoa, he added even more butter and sugar?

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.390
I’m sure he added the normal amount before...

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.340
If he makes the flavor too strong...

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:27.560
Oh, I see...

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:31.570
Dough that contains a lot of water will
lose an equivalent amount of taste.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.570
So naturally...!

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.890
A bold flavor...

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:37.570
A deeper flavor is possible.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:43.330
Wow, they look delicious.

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.830
Let’s begin the tasting.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.340
Now, starting with Kawachi-san’s Parisian.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.850
Kawachi-san, I think this is quite nice.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.650
Don’t you think?

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.850
Well, since I have a firm foundation,
something like this is a cinch.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.080
Well then, continuing with Azuma-san’s Parisian.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.110
Okay!

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.820
T-This is...?!

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:25.180
Right now, at this moment, my feelings
are without a doubt...

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.830
Parisian.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:32.360
This is Japan, but within my mouth,
a refined Paris is spreading.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.860
But then again, what makes us Parisian?

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.980
It’s painful to admit,
but this is really good.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:43.810
Its taste is certainly more defined
than the bread I made.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.530
Yes, it’s very delicious.

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:47.450
Yay!

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:48.560
However...

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.700
Whether or not we can place this in the store as it is...

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.750
cannot be decided by me.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.030
I need to get the manager’s opinion.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.490
Manager?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.840
Manager?! Aren’t you the manager?

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:04.170
You’re the granddaughter of the president of Azusagawa Corporation,

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.880
who owns the Pantasia chain, right?

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.670
You should be the most important person here.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:13.880
I may be his granddaughter, but such a role
is impossible for a young girl like me.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.690
To sum it up, let’s just say I’m the manager’s proxy.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:21.890
Besides, the current manager, Matsushiro
Ken-san, is a magnificent person.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.390
Oh, really...?

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:28.030
Well, they say he’s Japan’s number
one French bread artisan, after all.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:28.390
Ja-

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.900
Japan’s number one?!

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:35.290
Compared to me, and even Kuroyanagi-san
from the main store, he’s like a master.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:39.400
A master compared to that cruel and
heartless examiner, Kuroyanagi?

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.250
He must be an unbelievable
bread artisan!

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.500
I want to meet him right away!

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.620
I want him to try my bread!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:48.020
Where can I go meet him?

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.420
What is it?

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:54.630
You’re planning on getting on the manager’s
good side, ahead of me?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.650
I won’t let you do that.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:58.390
I’m going, too.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.420
O-Oh, right.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:03.890
I’ll be recognized by the manager,
and get closer to the top!

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.690
Hey, where can I go meet him?

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:09.640
Well, right now, he’d probably...

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.570
be with the horse.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.360
Horse?

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:16.870
An amusement park!

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:17.710
Uh, why?

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:18.580
Close!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.400
That was close?

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.300
I see...

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:34.460
So this is a race track.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.600
It wasn’t close at all...

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.470
Well, I suppose it may be an adult’s amusement park.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:44.180
However, would the manager
really be in a place like this?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.440
Chomp!!

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.200
Shall we ask that occhan lying over there?

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:09.240
Um, excuse me...

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.720
Occhan, occhan!

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.960
You can hear us, right?
You occhan with an afro.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:31.090
Hey, don’t use such
unnecessary adjectives!

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:31.730
Hey...

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.070
what’s that you’re holding?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.730
You can tell by looking, can’t you?

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.030
It’s French bread.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:39.730
Oh?

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.780
Sorry, but could you please share some with me?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.740
Just a bit is fine.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.120
What, are you hungry?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.240
Oh well... In that case, help yourself.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.500
I only need one,
so you can have this. Eat it.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.630
No, half is fine then.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.250
Smells good, doesn’t it?

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.280
W-What’re you doing?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.540
As I expected.
Even the horse won’t eat it.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.880
Perhaps you’ve poisoned it?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.080
Did you intend to give bread like that to a human?

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.630
You murderer!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.170
What?!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:44.170
Who’s a murderer?
Horses don’t eat bread in the first place.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.770
They don’t, eh?

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.180
Ah, so you had your own bread?

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:04.990
Delicious!

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:07.740
The horse ate the bread!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:12.830
You guys... Did you really think that
horses only eat carrots and straw?

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:18.500
You know, horses also feed on
grains like barley and wheat.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.340
If anything, they love it.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:23.010
However, although it’s okay when they need energy,

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:25.590
if you give them too much, they’ll become terribly ill.

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:29.120
So you do take care to control their diet,

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:33.840
but they are instinctively able to tell the
difference between good and bad foods.

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:36.140
What is it?

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.310
Hm, what’s that?

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.350
Seriously?

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.840
The horse says,

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.340
“Your bread tastes no good,”

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:47.390
“you definitely cannot sell that
at Pantasia’s southern Tokyo branch.”

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.860
“Don’t make a fool of me by thinking
the manager is a horse.”

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.740
Hihiin.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:52.910
That’s what he’s saying.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:55.410
T-The manager is a horse?!

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:59.650
On top of that, the manager horse
said that my bread tastes bad!

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.030
As if the horse could be the manager.

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:03.700
You’re the manager, aren’t you?

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.370
Is it really the horse?

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:05.710
I’m saying, that’s not it!

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:07.210
Manager
I’m saying, that’s not it!

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:07.420
I’m saying, that’s not it!

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:11.080
The fact that he knows about
Pantasia is the biggest hint.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.390
But how did he know we were from Pantasia?

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:17.170
What’s this we’re wearing?

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:18.920
Pantasia’s employee uniforms.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.440
Did Tsukino inform you of this place?

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:27.400
That young girl, hiring two seemingly
useless brats again...

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:30.470
This person is Matsushiro Ken.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:33.140
The man who can bake Japan’s
number one French bread.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:36.450
Even a horse will eat Japan’s number one French bread.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:37.450
Incredible!

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.960
You’re an incredible person!

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.200
Oh?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.210
You’ve got good eyes.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.870
I-In any case...

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:51.180
If the horse won’t even eat
Azuma’s bread...

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.430
Perhaps even a pony wouldn’t eat mine...

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:55.890
Listen up, you guys!

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.100
The horse said this, too.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:03.160
“We can’t put our name on bread
that’s just delicious.”

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.860
“Make a delicious bread!” is what he said.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.180
Right!

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:11.610
He says “right!” so easily...
but what on earth is “delicious bread?”

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:17.620
You see, we bread artisans... need to be creators.

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:21.480
A creator is someone who uses
his head to make things.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:25.130
If you neglect that, and just make bread...

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:28.130
Err, it’s the same as that.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.670
Sushi robot!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.590
Ultimately, you’re bread robots!

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.800
Your hands and machines would be one and the same.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:44.850
Who’s...

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.560
a machine?!

00:16:47.010 --> 00:16:48.970
I’m a human with blood
flowing through me.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:51.570
Then make the blood flow through your bread as well!

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:54.370
Regardless of those who eat it,

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.620
you must keep them in mind when you make your bread.

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.580
I’ll give you another chance.

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:03.120
Bring a delicious bread here tomorrow.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:03.900
Delicious bread

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.240
W-What’s that supposed to mean?

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:09.290
Something obvious. Just you try
bringing bad bread again...

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.800
You’ll be fired.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:13.790
Fired?!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.060
He was a wonderful person, wasn’t he? The manager.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:20.810
What part of him was?! The way he looks,
the things he said, it was all messed up!

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:24.130
Thanks to him, we’re suddenly risking unemployment.

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:28.650
Now, now... In any case, the manager’s
French bread is the greatest.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:42.020
The crust on the surface is so
crispy, the inside all fluffy...

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.020
As a single bread, it’s delicious twice-over.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.620
This bread is certainly a revolution
of the bread industry!

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:51.290
It definitely has depth, and plenty of body.
It’s the ultimate French bread.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.800
D-Delicious...

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.120
Even so, what’s the difference?

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:00.010
Even Azuma’s bread was about as tasty as this.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:03.170
Despite that, why does the horse only eat this bread?

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:06.730
Ahh, so he’s been talking about bread
a horse will eat again, after all?

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:08.890
You... were able to make it?

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:12.340
No way...

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:13.280
That was lame...

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:15.680
Horses, which are herbivorous animals,

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:20.240
seem to dislike the food additives
and excess fat in butter.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:24.240
Azuma-san, you put butter in your bread, right?

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:25.650
Yeah.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:27.740
You’re saying that that’s why it wouldn’t eat ours?

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:31.790
I don’t know about horses eating butter,
but people happily eat it, don’t they?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:36.010
Sure, they may not put much
butter in real French bread...

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:39.550
But our customers are Japanese,
not horses.

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:44.880
Certainly, since it’s French bread for the
Japanese people, who love softness...

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:48.380
I think it’s wrong to scold you, and
forbid you from using butter.

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:50.520
Isn’t it fine if it tastes good to people?

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.180
Why would we make it for a horse?

00:18:53.180 --> 00:18:57.280
I believe the manager is concerned about allergies.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:04.030
A long time ago, because of an allergic reaction
to dairy products, the manager’s sister...

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:07.650
N-No way...

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:10.040
That was 8 years ago...

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:13.660
Back when the manager was still
at the Pantasia main store.

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:16.920
Onii-chan!

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:18.910
Kaede.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.540
You came here to play again?

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:23.370
This is a battlefield, not a playground.

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.750
Saying those mean things again...

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:28.060
Ah, what’s this?
A new type of bread?

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:29.920
Looks delicious!

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:32.930
Yes, we plan to put them in store starting tomorrow.

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:34.560
I see, in that case...

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.280
Before then, I’ll...

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:38.430
sample some of it!

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:39.280
Hey!

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:42.780
Geez...

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:56.000
K-Kaede?

00:19:58.490 --> 00:19:59.920
Kaede!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.960
Kariya General Hospital

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:05.760
Anaphylactic shock?
Note: “Anaphylaxis” / “anaphylactic shock” is a severe, whole-body allergic reaction.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.770
It’s said to be the most extreme allergic reaction.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.080
In the case of food,

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:14.720
we see it occurring with dairy products such as milk and butter, or eggs.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:17.980
It’s been 7 years since my sister was born.
Nothing like this has ever happened.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:20.440
There are some cases where there is degeneration,

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.490
even though the person
shows no symptoms.

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:25.940
You’ll need to be careful from now on.

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:29.490
In any case, she’s out of critical danger.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:32.360
Her condition is now stable.

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:36.700
However... if treatment had come just a little later...

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:41.540
it would have surely been life-threatening.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:49.300
Onii-chan.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:52.130
Kaede!

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:55.770
I wonder what happened to me...

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:59.190
Ah, that’s right, Onii-chan...

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.140
Umm...

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:02.780
Umm.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.600
It was delicious...

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:09.790
Your bread is definitely the best in Japan.

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:11.780
Damn it!

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:17.610
My sister’s body had become one that rejects
dairy products, without us realizing it...

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:22.920
Although I didn’t know, I... almost made
bread that left me without a sister.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:29.990
Making bread dough soft while giving it flavor is simple

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.310
if you add dairy products such as milk and butter.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:38.130
However, while there are still people with
allergic reactions to dairy products,

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:42.640
he aims to make bread that anybody can eat
safely, no matter how difficult it may be.

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.560
“Never give up,” he says.

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:50.900
He probably asks such unreasonable things
of us, because he has such feelings.

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:54.530
In particular, for frequently eaten
breads such as French bread,

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:57.540
its effect on people is no trivial matter.

00:21:57.950 --> 00:22:00.040
Right now, that little sister is...?

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:02.660
She is well.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:06.500
She even comes here often, seeking
the manager’s bread.

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:08.500
I got it.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:13.060
In other words, the “delicious bread”
the manager speaks of...

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:16.550
is made without milk or butter,
all without sacrificing flavor,

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:18.190
while bringing good health and good taste together...

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:18.550
Bread Workshop
while bringing good health and good taste together...

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:20.270
The ultimate bread, right?
Bread Workshop

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:23.480
Isn’t it?

00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:30.940
His little sister...

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:33.620
Little sister...

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:47.610
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:56.620
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:23:00.180 --> 00:23:07.630
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:12.790
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:18.930
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:21.510
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:25.650
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:30.420
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:34.260
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:38.950
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:44.120
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:44.390 --> 00:23:52.930
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:53.330 --> 00:24:02.300
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:09.100
We’ve created bread that even a horse would eat.

00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:10.320
Right, Azuma?

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:13.100
It’s Hanako’s breast milk...

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:14.720
Hanako?!

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:16.890
Next episode, Yakitate!! Japan.

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:17.940
Delicious!!

00:24:17.940 --> 00:24:19.850
A Decisively Ultimate Butter!

00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:20.930
It’s Hanako!

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:23.690
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:27.320
French bread is named differently, depending on size.

00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:29.400
Their standard size was decided

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:32.670
by the emperor of France at the time, Napoleon Bonaparte!

00:24:33.030 --> 00:24:34.920
It’s “très bien!”
